Design a programmable logic array (PLA) that processes a 4-bit input to generate a 2-bit output. The module computes four product terms based on combinations of the input bits, implementing specific logical AND operations, and then combines these product terms into two sum terms using logical OR operations. The output is determined by the evaluated sum terms, where out[0] indicates the first sum term and out[1] indicates the second, allowing for the creation of custom logic functions based on the input configuration.
module top_module(
  input [3:0] in,
  output [1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [3:0] in,
  output [1:0] out
);parameter p = 4; // number of product terms
parameter q = 2; // number of sum terms

// product terms
wire prod1 = in[0] & in[1];
wire prod2 = in[2] & ~in[3];
wire prod3 = in[0] & in[2] & ~in[3];
wire prod4 = in[1] & in[2] & in[3];

// sum terms
wire sum1 = prod1 | prod2;
wire sum2 = prod3 | prod4;

// output signals
assign out[0] = sum1;
assign out[1] = sum2;

endmodule

