description:
Design a parity generator that computes the parity of a given n-bit input data signal. The module accepts an n-bit input and outputs a single parity bit, which can be configured to produce either even or odd parity based on the specified parameter. The output parity bit is generated by XORing all bits of the input data together, and the final parity output is determined by inverting the result if odd parity is required.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] data_in,
  output reg parity_out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] data_in,
  output reg parity_out
);parameter n = 8; // number of data bits
parameter parity_type = "even"; // even or odd parity

integer i;
reg [n-1:0] data_bits;
reg parity_bit;

always @(*) begin
  data_bits = data_in;
  parity_bit = data_bits[0];

  for (i = 1; i < n; i = i + 1) begin
    parity_bit = parity_bit ^ data_bits[i];
  end

  if (parity_type == "odd") begin
    parity_out = ~parity_bit;
  end else begin
    parity_out = parity_bit;
  end
end

endmodule

