Design a circuit that computes the absolute value of an 8-bit signed number. The circuit takes an 8-bit input (input_num) and a 1-bit input (input_sign) representing the sign of the number; if input_sign is 1 (indicating a negative number), it outputs the two's complement of input_num, effectively converting it to its positive equivalent. If input_sign is 0, it simply passes the input_num as the output.
